meta {
  name: Get Details by TMDB ID
  type: http
  seq: 8
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/tmdb/details/{{tmdbId}}?language={{language}}
  body: none
  auth: none
}

params:query {
  language: {{language}}
}

docs {
  # Get Details by TMDB ID

  Resolves details for a numeric TMDB ID when the caller does not know in advance whether the ID corresponds to a movie or a TV series.
  The server first attempts `movieDetails(tmdbId)` and, if not found, falls back to `tvDetails(tmdbId)`, augmenting the response with `media_type: "movie" | "tv"`.

  ## Path Parameters
  | Parameter | Type | Required | Description |
  | --- | --- | --- | --- |
  | `tmdbId` | `number` | Yes | Numeric TMDB identifier. |

  ## Query Parameters
  | Parameter | Type | Required | Default | Description |
  | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
  | `language` | `string` | No | `en-US` | Localization language tag. |

  ## Responses
  - **200 OK**: TMDB details object with an added `media_type` field (`"movie"` or `"tv"`).
  - **400 Bad Request**: `{ "error": "tmdbId must be a number" }`.
  - **404 Not Found**: `{ "error": "Not found" }`.
  - **500 Internal Server Error**: `{ "error": "<message>" }`.
}

